According to the complaint that was filed last month against the parts maker, the airbags @CORPFULL supplied to the auto companies had a number of defects, including a tendency to unexpectedly deploy, with explosive force that sometimes injured or decapitated passengers, and often FAILED to deploy during crashes, or did so, but exploded with deadly force in many instances, or only deployed several seconds after the crash had occurred, adding to any injuries already sustained by the passengers. In many of the cases where the bags deployed, passengers were also injured by shrapnel from the bags, even if not otherwise harmed.

