@CORPFULL WITHDRAWS ITS HIGHLY SUCCESSFUL "NO-COUNT" ARTIFICIALLY-SWEETENED BEVERAGES FROM MARKET

@CORPFULL announced today that it will cease all sales of its beverages containing the controversial artificial sweetener, "No-Count" (made by Toxico Chemicals). The petroleum-based sweetener has fueled a tremendous sales boom in @CORPFULL's soft drinks in recent months, but a verdict by a California jury has upheld claims by litigants that No-Count causes severe, irreparable liver and kidney damage and, in many cases, liver cancer (invariably fatal).

Washington sources say that the introduction of the sweetener without prior FDA approval or testing was only possible because of the heavy lobbying clout in the U.S. Congress by its maker, Toxico Chemicals, which has close Defense Department ties and also makes chemical weapons for the Army. No-Count was the first non-military product made by Toxico in the D.O.D.'s new "Swords to Plowshares" program of research grants.

Soft drink industry analysts say @CORPFULL has severely damaged its once-impeccable image among consumers....

