@CORPFULL PROFITS HANDSOMELY FROM ITS OPERATIONS IN ISTANBUL; CITES ITS CLOSE TIES TO THE TURKISH GOVERNMENT

@CORPFULL is one of the few companies that has @MISC been able to operate very profitably in Turkey, and which has somehow been able to overcome the many obstacles Turkey places before any company that wishes to import mundane items into the country, such as shoes. The company cites its very close and amicable ties with the government, and special tax breaks it has been able to negotiate with the Ankara government on its operations in Turkey, as the main sources of its resounding success in penetrating the always difficult Turkish marketplace.

Human rights advocates in @COUNTRY are very skeptical about the company's record of success in Turkey, however. Some suggest that it is more of a function of the company having given in to official blackmail, by breaking off its endorsement contracts with a popular Kurdish singer who was considered an "enemy of the state" and terrorist by Turkey, before his tragic and unsolved murder in @FACT last month.

